<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScarlandsMarkLock.xml            UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §2 attachment route, RESOLVED by the spike pass
  (2026-09-14, finding 4): no MapComponent of this kit's own is needed —
  RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml (same folder) already proves
  <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent> in a biome's own
  <biomeMapConditions> is enough (BiomeConditionMapComponent.MapGenerated ->
  GameConditionMaker.MakeConditionPermanent, decompile-confirmed that pass).
  This file copies that shape verbatim onto RUT_Scarlands.xml's own
  biomeMapConditions (see that file's own header for the wiring).

  No forcedWeather here — unlike the Miasma's lock, the Scarlands mark isn't
  a weather effect; RUT_Scarlands.xml keeps its own baseWeatherCommonalities
  untouched. onlyUnroofed=false is deliberate and the one field this pass
  changed from RC4's own default (true): the mark is "every colonist who
  walks the Scarlands" (kit spec's own words) — a roof over your head doesn't
  un-mark you, unlike the Miasma's breath-tax which IS a roof problem.

  hediffSeverityPerInterval/damageIntervalTicks: see RUT_ScarlandsMark.xml's
  own header for the full +0.2/day-on-map derivation (0.3 gross this
  condition adds per day, netting against that hediff's own -0.1/day
  HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay comp). 2500 ticks (~1 in-game hour)
  reuses MIASMA_MECHANICS_1's own INVENTED-BUILD scan cadence rather than
  inventing a second one.

  carrierHediff deliberately NOT set: EnvironmentalWeatherExtension.
  ConfigErrors refuses carrierHediff == hediffToApply (double-applies
  severity) and there is no second hediff here for a carrier to bootstrap
  the way Miasma's exposure comp needed one — hediffToApply alone is
  correct and sufficient (HealthUtility.AdjustSeverity, decompile-confirmed,
  creates the hediff on first positive application).

  MayRequire is load-bearing: conditionClass and the modExtension both live
  in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScarlandsMarkLock</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>the Scarlands' weight</label>
    <description>Something in this ground gets under the skin and stays there. Every hour spent walking the Scarlands leaves its mark a little deeper.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>true</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <hediffToApply>RUT_ScarlandsMark</hediffToApply>
        <hediffSeverityPerInterval>0.0125</hediffSeverityPerInterval>
        <damageIntervalTicks>2500</damageIntervalTicks>
        <onlyUnroofed>false</onlyUnroofed>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
